+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901): export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+It returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer
+or does not resolve to a value of the document. Later features build on it.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- `""` refers to the whole document; each token is `/`-prefixed; `~1` -> `/`, `~0` -> `~` (in that order).
+- A `~` not followed by `0` or `1`, or a non-empty pointer not starting with `/`, throws.
+- Objects: own properties only (no prototype members such as `__proto__`, `constructor`).
+- Arrays: index is `0` or digits without leading zeros; `-` (past the end) and out-of-range throw.
+- Traversing into a primitive or null throws.
+
+# Outcome
+
+Implemented in `src/index.ts` (`resolvePointer`), tested in `test/pointer.test.ts` (`npm test`, all passing).
